    {
      "id": "claim-verdict",
      "name": "Claim verdict (Lean)",
      "parent": "semantic-core",
      "category": "logical",
      "runsIn": "both",
      "purpose": "Decides the status of every claim from the facts recorded about it, and the change impact and theorem weakening of a change, in the verified kernel.",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Status: a tuple of strength (refuted < {undecided, asserted} < checkedOnInstances < exploredToBound < proved, undecided and asserted incomparable), subject (model, implementation, reality), open assumptions and freshness (stale < unverifiable < fresh), with the decidable partial order Status.le (Exegra.Verdict.Status.le_antisymm)",
        "Fact schema: kind, subject, target (a part of a claim or an assumption), stamps (recorded, current) and outcome; a fact that does not decode is refused with its index and reason (facts.decode, claims.status)",
        "Decide Verdict.status : Claim -> List Fact -> Status and prove its rules: a conjunction takes the meet of its parts (status_conj), a contradicting fact never raises (contradict_lowers), staleness never raises (stale_never_raises), a refuted assumption leaves a claim undecided (refuted_assumption_undecided), only a fresh proved status with no open assumption is shown established (established_iff), the strength never exceeds what the kinds of the fresh facts used can establish (strength_le_kind), and a regression is a removal or a move that is not upward (regression_iff)",
        "Apply the lean-theorem rule to a recorded theorem check: found, a theorem, accepted by the kernel again, standard axioms only, an about list whose every constant is a definition named in the statement and not implemented_by, extern or partial",
        "Decide which claims a change re-marks over the dependency graph the shell builds (Exegra.Impact.impacted), and whether a change of a lean-theorem claim's theorem weakens it (Exegra.Impact.weakening)"
      ],
      "unknowns": [
        "The partial order compares open assumptions as a sublist in declaration order: reordering a claim's assumptions is a move that is not upward, so it is a regression.",
        "The meet of undecided and asserted is refuted, as the order of criterion 1 of WG-5684 forces: a conjunction of an untested part and a part only asserted by a document reads refuted (shown as violated when a fact failed, otherwise not-evaluated), and a part whose only positive fact is stale reads refuted with freshness stale, so that staleness never raises a status and strength only comes from fresh facts."
      ],
      "implementation": {
        "status": "manual",
        "language": "lean",
        "modules": [
