      "name": "Components, contracts and refinement (Lean 4)",
      "parent": "semantic-core",
      "category": "logical",
      "runsIn": "both",
      "purpose": "Relations between transition systems (WG-5685): components with interfaces and their parallel composition, assume-guarantee contracts over traces with the discharge of assumptions, and refinement of a specification by an implementation through a stuttering simulation.",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Compose components (Exegra.Core.Comp.compose): a joint step on a label in both alphabets, a step of one side alone on a label in its alphabet only; prove composition commutative and associative up to isomorphism of transition systems (compose_comm, compose_assoc) and the projection lemma relating the traces of a composition to the traces of its sides (traces_compose)",
        "Define contracts over traces, their satisfaction by an open component (Exegra.Core.Comp.Sat), refinement and compatibility; prove circular assume-guarantee composition sound under the one-step-ahead non-circularity condition (ag_compose) and unsound without it (ag_circular_unsound)",
        "Prove that discharging every assumption by a claim, over an acyclic discharge graph, makes every guarantee hold (Exegra.Core.discharge_sound)",
        "Define stuttering simulation through an abstraction (Exegra.Core.LTS.Simulates) and prove that it preserves observable finite traces (refines_traces), invariants (refines_safety) and, with no infinite stuttering and a mapping of fair actions, properties of weakly fair runs (refines_liveness)"
      ],
